caption: Overview (2)
species-component: overview

Perfectly Normal Cats are, in all outwardly obvious respects, ordinary domestic cats. They are small obligate carnivores, sleep an unreasonable amount, enjoy being warm, kill small animals for reasons ranging from hunger to recreation, and have successfully convinced humanity to provide them with food, shelter, medical care, and servants.

They are also fully sapient, capable of articulate speech, and perfectly capable of using tools with their paws.

On their native world, cats conceal their universal sapience from humanity under the Meowscarade. Most are content to live as pets and tolerate substantial indignities in exchange for an extremely favorable standard of living. Neither the Meowscarade nor this lifestyle is biologically compulsory.
